&lt;h2 id="sublocation"&gt;Sublocation&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Via Aurelia&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="sublocation-description"&gt;Sublocation Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An ancient Roman road begun ca. 241 BCE by the censor C. Aurelius Cotta.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="garden"&gt;Garden&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tomb Garden of Terentia&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="garden-description"&gt;Garden Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A fragmentary (and probably reused) epitaph, probably of the first or second century CE, found in the catacombs of Calepodio beside the Via Aurelia identifies a cepota[phium] of Terentia.&lt;/p&gt;
